title: "THE USE OF DIFFERENT TOOLS FOR BIOFLUORESCENCE ANALYSIS: CALIBRATING THE RELIABILITY OF ANALYSIS METHODS"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-02-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/brunopiato/hippocampus_reidi"
keywords:
  - biofluorescence
  - Hippocampus reidi
  - Syngnathiformes
  - analysis methods
  - animal behavior
  - biological communication
  - light emission
  - scientific methodology
  - image-analysis
  - python-script
abstract: >-
  This repositoy provides a Python-based script and standardized methods for 
  analyzing biofluorescence images in marine organisms. Developed using 
  Hippocampus reidi as a model, the tool evaluates biofluorescent hues and 
  patterns, facilitating research into stress responses, predation, and 
  evolutionary distribution of biofluorescence in bony fish.
